LOCK A (verifyTimeoutMs default): today a lock draft without an explicit verifyTimeoutMs silently gets 60s, which no real Swift chain fits — this caused two slips today. Measured seam first: find where the default is applied (draft creation / run). Fix: the drafter must require the field or estimate it from the verifyCommand contents (xcodebuild present ⇒ ≥3600000), never silently default to 60s. Fail-first pin: drafting without the field either errors or gets a sane estimate — assert it.